{"availability":"available","full":"Andersseen/and-web-components","name":"and-web-components","description":"Modular UI stack for any framework — 25 accessible web components, headless state machines, CSS layout, motion, DOM behaviors and 88 icons. Every package installs on its own.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-07T20:06:30Z","updated":"2026-10-08T12:02:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://libs.andersseen.dev","topics":["a11y","accessibility","angular","astro","component-library","css-framework","custom-elements","design-system","headless-ui","monorepo","react","shadow-dom","stenciljs","tailwindcss","typescript","ui-components","vue","web-components"],"demo":"https://and-web-components-demo.pages.dev/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T19:03:32.614Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T19:03:32.614Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T19:03:32.614Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T19:03:32.614Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Vue","Angular"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Headless state machines, DOM behaviors, layout primitives, motion, icons and 25 accessible components — each published on its own. Adopt only the layers you need. Works in Angular, React, Vue, Astro, Svelte, or a plain HTML file.","Most component libraries are all-or-nothing: you want a grid helper, you install a runtime, a theme, and 40 components you'll never render. And Libs splits that into layers you can take individually.","An Angular app that only wants attribute-driven layout installs @andersseen/layout — pure CSS, no JS runtime, no components. A team building its own design system takes @andersseen/headless-components and skips every styled package. @andersseen/layout, @andersseen/motion, @andersseen/behaviors, @andersseen/icon and @andersseen/headless-components have zero in-repo dependencies and work standalone. @andersseen/web-components (and its generated Angul